  "findings": [
    "Platform and ramps in checked colored variants use one glTF material named platformer, one mesh primitive and one shared platformer_texture.png. Their blue regions are NOT a separately addressable material slot in source.",
    "Button and floor/wall lever have separately named child meshes but share the same platformer atlas material. Mesh-scoped override is possible after material cloning, but blue surfaces within that mesh require texture/UV mask or per-face geometry split.",
    "Conveyor extra has two independent glTF primitives/materials: platformer (platformer_texture.png) and threads (threads.png). Its belt material is a particularly low-risk selective animation target without changing the hard frame.",
    "Saw trap has separately named sawblade child but its entire asset still uses one shared platformer atlas; mesh-scoped override requires material cloning and collider-safe animation.",
    "Original different color variants each declare the same platformer material name and platformer_texture.png filename, with color expressed by image content and/or mapped UVs. Material.name alone cannot identify blue vs red regions.",
    "Use the exact source material index and primitive identity; cloned per-instance material or selected primitive replacement must not leak changes to all instances sharing cached source material.",
    "Any use of KFB moving terrain color-band shader needs true semantic/UV mask after BIN+PNG intake, source render proof, pass-through of original PBR texture, and visual/combat/collider separation."
  ],
  "nextGate": "WS0_PLATFORMER_ASSET_INTAKE_AND_L01_SOURCE_GATE"
}
